{{also|pus}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|po͝os}}, {{IPA|en|/pʊs/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-puss.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʊs}}

===Etymology 1===
Probably from {{der|en|gml|pūs}}, {{m|gml|pūskatte}} or {{der|en|nl|poes||puss, cat”, slang for “vulva}}, ultimately from a common {{der|en|gem}} word for cat, perhaps ultimately {{onomatopoeic|en|title=imitative}} of a sound made to get its attention (compare Arabic [[بسة]]). 

Akin to {{cog|fy|poes}}, {{cog|nds|Puus}}, {{m|nds|Puuskatte}}, {{cog|da|pus}}, dialectal {{cog|sv|kattepus}}, {{cog|no|pus}}.

Found also in several other European, North African and West Asian languages; compare {{cog|ro|pisică}} and {{cog|sc|pisittu}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|es}}

# {{lb|en|informal|often as a term of address}} A [[cat]].
#: {{ux|en|Our local theatre is showing '''Puss''' in Boots.}}
#: {{ux|en|Come here, '''puss'''! I've got some milk for you.}}
# {{lb|en|dated|affectionate}} A [[girl]] or young [[woman]], or any [[child]].
# {{lb|en|dated|hunting}} A [[hare]].
#* {{RQ:Fielding Tom Jones}}
#*: He then began to beat about, in the same language and in the same manner as if he had been beating for a hare; and at last cried out, "Soho! '''Puss''' is not far off. Here's her form, upon my soul; I believe I may cry stole away."
# {{lb|en|vulgar|slang}} The [[vulva]] (female [[genitalia]]).
# {{lb|en|vulgar|slang|chiefly|_|North America}} A [[coward]]; a [[wuss]]; someone who is unable to stand up for him- or herself.

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|cat}} {{l|en|moggie}}/[[moggy]]

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|en|pussy}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|puss moth}}
* {{l|en|puss out}}

===Etymology 2===
Of {{der|en|cel|-}} origin, from or akin to {{der|en|ga|pus||mouth, lip}}, from {{der|en|mga|bus|}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|es}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} The [[mouth]].
#: ''She gave him a slap in the '''puss'''.''
#* '''1991''', ''New York Magazine'' (volume 24, number 21, page 62)
#*: Hubbert has a rasping voice and a razory laugh, and he's busy and theatrical in the worst way — a noisy performing pro with whirlwind arms and a saturnine '''puss'''.

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|mouth}} {{l|en|cakehole}}, {{l|en|gob}}, {{l|en|mush}}, {{l|en|trap}}

